        "original_id": "54e67148-dc00-59dc-bcd2-25fbc27f43a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Belgium, Europe\n- Events: Thirty Years' War\n- Concepts: battlefield of Europe, cockpit of Europe, cockfight, cockpit\n\nFacts:\n- The Thirty Years' War lasted from 1618 to 1648.\n- Since the Thirty Years' War, Belgium has often been called the \"battlefield of Europe\" because of its strategic location and the many armies that fought on its soil.\n- Since the Thirty Years' War, Belgium has also often been called the \"cockpit of Europe.\"\n- A cockfight is a blood sport between two cocks, or gamecocks.\n- A cockpit is the ring where a cockfight is held.",
